  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For electromagnetic wave speed of light is given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br />Electric field is expressed as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mtext>to&#160;direction</mtext><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mtext>and&#160;direction</mtext><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math><br /><br />The expression of electric field is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
